<article class="env-lemma" id="08EP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08EP">Lemma <span data-tag="08EP">36.14.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $U \subset X$ be an open subscheme. Let $(T, E, m)$ be a triple as in Definition <a href="/tag/08EM" data-tag="08EM">36.14.1</a>. If </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$T \subset U$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
approximation holds for $(T, E|_ U, m)$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the sheaves $H^ i(E)$ for $i \geq m$ are supported on $T$, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> then approximation holds for $(T, E, m)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $j : U \to X$ be the inclusion morphism. If $P \to E|_ U$ is an approximation of the triple $(T, E|_ U, m)$ over $U$, then $j_!P = Rj_*P \to j_!(E|_ U) \to E$ is an approximation of $(T, E, m)$ over $X$. See Cohomology, Lemmas <a href="/tag/08DF" data-tag="08DF">20.33.6</a> and <a href="/tag/08DP" data-tag="08DP">20.49.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>